BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.87 Tm (on production data. State commission sites update monthly and 'may lag a couple of months,' so a May) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 529.65 Tm (lookup may only surface February or March volumes, and a brand-new well may not show at all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 514.42 Tm ([Yy7az5T7_vs @ 00:13:41]. Price is the next leak. Sands notes that Bakken barrels can clear at 50 dollars) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.20 Tm (when WTI prints 60, because of a price differential tied to transport and processing costs, and that operator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.97 Tm (hedging blurs the average price on the check stub further [Yy7az5T7_vs @ 00:16:47]. The AAPL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 468.75 Tm (study-guide trap is premature math. In Situation #5, a 1/8 lease minus Charlie's 3% NPRI would net David) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 453.52 Tm (9.5%, but no lease exists yet. The instructor says 'don't be thinking the answer to this is 9.5%,' because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 438.30 Tm (correct answer is 100% minerals subject to the 3% NPRI [HkEK5QVZAJ0 @ 00:04:30]. Each of these errors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.07 Tm (produces a clean-looking decimal that is simply wrong.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.85 Tm (The second failure mode is fat-fingering decimals, and the instructors commit it live on camera. While) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.62 Tm (checking the four Brady heirs' joint-ownership total, the Land Training instructor stalls mid-multiplication with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.40 Tm ('oh I did that wrong sorry.' It takes a third pass before 0.03125 times four reconciles back to the original 1/8) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.17 Tm (royalty [pjP04Ns4pww @ 00:06:07]. In Pooled Unit Problem 4, a one-fifth royalty on 10 acres inside an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.95 Tm (80-acre Marcellus drilling and spacing unit correctly computes to 0.025. It then gets restated aloud as 'a 0.25) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.72 Tm (is the net revenue interest,' a tenfold slip that would wreck a pay deck if it reached a division order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.50 Tm ([kC2dYFP0U0g @ 00:01:26]. In the unit co-tenant lesson, the calculator returns 014063 for Peter's royalty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 301.27 Tm (share in the 640-acre unit, and the whiteboard receives 01463, a dropped zero that silently shifts the figure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.05 Tm ([n2pg2-Q06P8 @ 00:06:59]. Alyce Hoge explains why slips like these hide so well. Division order decimals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.82 Tm ('usually go out to eight decimal places,' which is how owners end up staring at 'crazy decimals' they cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.60 Tm (eyeball [eZU5hvGcngg @ 00:13:51]. The practitioner fix is structural: separate factor columns, Excel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.37 Tm (formulas copied down the sheet, and a closing sum that must reconcile.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.15 Tm (The third failure mode is running a check that cannot catch the error. The UHD instructor's paycheck) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.92 Tm (analogy is blunt: if the payroll person botches a deduction, take-home pay is wrong. Likewise, 'if we make a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.70 Tm (mistake anywhere before we get to the net it will affect the net revenue interest' [oHKF06pFkh0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.47 Tm (00:04:15]. The same instructor caps the method with a warning. When an operator brings five leases with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.25 Tm (different burdens into one unit, 'you can't co-mingle them.' The check has to run lease by lease, or it will not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.02 Tm (return the gross-minus-burdens figure [oHKF06pFkh0 @ 00:10:21]. The unit co-tenant lesson supplies a) Tj ET
