BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm ([tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:31:17]. The overpayment trap is where signing blind gets expensive. Blue Mesa Minerals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (reports that when an operator later finds it overpaid, owners can go months or years with no royalty revenue) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (while the account balances, and warns against any clause that puts the operator's errors on you, including) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (its legal fees [SfX6ycoYg24 @ 00:02:51]. Steven Hatcher says the real commitment in most states is not to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (the acreage but to repaying or indemnifying the operator for overpayment, handled through suspense until) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (recouped, and adds that operators have actually filed suit against lessors to recover funds [Z_HlEDh8-rw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (00:07:42]. Matt Sands spells out the temptation: a division order shows a bigger number than you think you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (own and you just cash the checks, until the operator discovers you own 0.05 percent instead of 0.1 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (withholds the difference until you make it whole [inopKiaG-3A @ 00:15:56]. The economics check is simple:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (a bigger decimal is not a windfall, it is a deferred clawback.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (The second trap rides in the fine print. Blue Mesa Minerals refuses to sign division orders carrying) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (cost-deduction language: if your lease is cost-free and the division order lets the operator deduct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (compression and cleaning costs, you have handed back what you negotiated, and Blue Mesa reports some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (operators taking 20 to 30 percent of royalties in deductions while others take up to 70 or 80 percent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm ([SfX6ycoYg24 @ 00:05:26]. Royalty Clerk flags the same extra in Texas, a clause letting the payer take) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (gathering, compression and processing costs whether or not your lease allows it, and notes such a term is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (invalid to the extent it contradicts the lease [DN-VIoSmyF0 @ 00:01:17]. Mineral View puts numbers on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (lease-driven bleed: $1.50 per barrel on 5,000 barrels a month strips $7,500 from the revenue base, and a 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (percent marketing fee on a $100,000 well removes $3,000 a month, or $36,000 a year, before royalty math) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (starts [KYu7M4t5LAk @ 00:06:54]. The tax-side leak is just as mechanical: skip the W-9 and NARO says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (the payer must withhold 28 percent of royalty income for the IRS, so send it no matter what [W3POOsq6ka0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (@ 00:01:31]. Each of these leaks repeats on every monthly check, so the deduction language gets read line) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (by line against the lease before anything is signed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (The third cluster is plain clerical failure. Blue Mesa Minerals has seen decimals typed with one zero too) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (many or too few, and errors that ran miscalculated for a long time until the owner did independent math) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm ([SfX6ycoYg24 @ 00:02:11]. Royalty Clerk lists the mistake versions of a changing decimal, a dropped digit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (or an old unit size, and shows why the fourth digit matters: on 10,000 barrels at $70, a decimal 2.7 percent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (low costs $18.59 a month on oil alone, while a lease promising 1/4 paid at the 1/8 number pays exactly half) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm ([blbomhUd0sA @ 00:02:45]. Matt Sands says that when a well changes hands the decimal should not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (change, and a mismatch is often the new operator loading its pay deck into accounting wrong, so compare) Tj ET
